<title>USA: Kingdom of Thailand sets $600 mln in yankee notes.</title>
<headline>Kingdom of Thailand sets $600 mln in yankee notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following $600 million yankee debt issue from the Kingdom of Thailand was priced on Thursday, said lead manager Lehman Brothers.</p>
<p>The offering was increased in size from an initial $500 million. The deal was co-led with underwriter Salomon Brothers.</p>
<p>BORROWER KINGDOM OF THAILAND</p>
<p>AMT  $600 MLN	COUPON  7.750     MATURITY  04/15/07</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.603  FIRST PAY DATE NA</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A3    YIELD   7.808     PAY FREQ  SEMI</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P     A     SPREAD  90 BP     CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1675))</p>
